17. Sandra needs eggs to make 15 flans.  She needs 3 eggs per flan, so she needs a total of 15 * 3 = 45 eggs.  Each time she babysits, she gets 9 eggs.  To find out how many times she needs to babysit, we divide the total number of eggs needed by the number of eggs she gets per babysitting: 45 / 9 = 5.  Therefore, Sandra has to babysit 5 times.  \boxed{5}

